    "body": "This is worth calling out. There *is* the existing note, but most readers will overlook the implications buried in the encoding jargon. As a suggestion, when you make the example, use characters that are more common and which are recommended. I'd suggest replacing U+FB00 (the `ff` ligature) with a character from the full/half-width forms block, such as U+FF5E (wave dash) or one of the wide letters, since the ligature is a compatibility character. I'd also suggest using your favorite emoji rather than an obscure character such as U+10478.",
